silm:instances_papers_21_ologs_and_typed_english_chapters_03_typed_verb_discipline_sections_02_verb_directionality_concrete_anchor_2_f_inv#isbodymassofarrow silm:hasLongDescription "The IsBodyMassOfArrow is the would-be inverse BodyMassQualityBox -> DomesticCatBox, only admitted with explicit inverse declaration. In the paper's apparatus it appears as the symbol 'f_inv', a concrete instance grounded in the Mittens domain story; it serves as the anchor whose semantics every diagram, formula, and prose reference back to." .
